      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e that code is self-contained though (a call to the external crate zeroize and a loop issuing DC instructions)\n\nI checked this code. There are lots of things to move actually\n\n- All the `flush*` functions in [libvmbase/src/memory/util.rs:l41-82](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/libvmbase/src/memory/util.rs;l\u003d41;drc\u003d1a089a0c4aab619039b208a087f4f441e4fa1425) need to be duplicated between `vmbase` and `lib_open_dice_clear_memory_baremetal`. Several functions are still used in other places so we still need to keep them in vmbase.\n- Some macro and util functions like `read_sysreg!` also needs to duplicate.\n\nIt\u0027s much simpler to just add one line in rialto tbh. Since we only have two usages like this, we can refactor it when there\u0027s a third usage (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rule_of_three_(computer_programming))",
